## What is Cronjob ?
A Cron job is a schedule task that allows you to run scripts or commands at a specified intervals. 

## Why use cron jobs ?
Cron jobs automates repetitive task ensuring they run at scheduled without manual intervention
Example = Backing up files, running system maintenance, or sending email reportes.

## How does Cron Work ?
Cron use a demon (a background process) called cron to execute cron tasks.
The configuration of these tasks is stored in a file called a Crontab.

